      "problem": "Find the value of $-15 \\div 3.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-15)$ by a positive one $\\color{blue}(3).$ So the result will be negative:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14147219/assets/22216a843f727403f0d0a4c179de7885622d0984d846626ca31cc6be1e4314d8.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $15$ by $3$ without any signs: $15 \\div 3 = 5.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-15)} \\div {\\color{blue}3} = {\\color{red}-5}.\n$$",
